{
  "delta_from_prior": "Replaces Neon103 (21 vars, 105 clauses, observed peak 1 due to an unbalanced 3-group right side collapsing early) and advances beyond Neon58 (20 vars, 108 clauses, monotone-split bipartite quotient, peak 8, 8.51s) with a 16-variable, 283-clause Overlapping Signed-Pair Transversal (OSPT-6) that compresses cleanly to 12 variables and 91 clauses (peak ~10 predicted, fast IALH-5), defeats both original and quotient core_refutation, and simultaneously breaks Fable95's CIMS-FK monotone-split assumption (obstruction >= 16 clauses) and Fable73's positive link-twin symmetry.",
  "explanation": "### 1. Audit of Pinned v5 (`blq-composed-core-scc-emra-ialh5-v5`)\nAuditing the supplied solver, `compression.py`, `core_refutation.py`, and pinned SCC/DP/MRA dependencies finds **no correctness bug**:\n- **`compression.py`**: `_verify_certificate` rebuilds blocks from every clause of `dense_formula(formula, ids)`, checks no duplicate variables per clause, checks `sum(counts) == len(quotient)`, verifies every referenced linear form is supported inside its block, checks `evaluate(clauses, x) == evaluate(q, image)` on all `2**len(support)` local assignments, and checks `parity(form & column) == int(i == j)` entrywise (proving surjectivity of the linear projection). Because `run_counting` normalizes first, accepted compressions are exact equisatisfiability certificates.\n- **`core_refutation.py`**: `probe` independently verifies `set(core).issubset(set(f))` and only returns `UNSAT` when `compress_root(core)` succeeds and `q` is an unsatisfiable 2-SAT formula checked by `two_sat`. Composing `probe` once on an accepted exact quotient preserves soundness.\n- **Residual solver (`run_counting_core`, `canon_plus`, `elim_plus`, `prune`)**: `refute` checks every IALH-5 dual certificate with exact `Fraction` arithmetic over full-formula UP tables; `prune` drops `g` only when `below(g, h)` holds (`models(g) <= models(h)`), preserving disjunction satisfiability.\n\n### 2. Fixture Construction: Overlapping Signed-Pair Transversal (OSPT-6)\nWe construct a 16-variable, 283-clause, width-<=8 UNSAT formula (full order `1..16`) whose **exact BLQ quotient** is a 12-variable, 91-clause, kernel-free, non-monotone-split residual contradiction:\n- **Logical pairs**: 6 pairs $P_i = (a_i, b_i)$ for $i \\in \\{1..6\\}$, mapped to original variables `1..16` via 4 disjoint XOR lifts:\n  - Unlifted (8 vars): `1`=$a_2$, `2`=$a_3$, `3`=$a_4$, `4`=$a_5$, `5`=$b_2$, `6`=$b_3$, `7`=$a_1$, `8`=$a_6$.\n  - Lifted (8 vars -> 4 XOR forms): $b_4 = 9 \\oplus 10$, $b_5 = 11 \\oplus 12$, $b_1 = 13 \\oplus 14$, $b_6 = 15 \\oplus 16$.\n- **Base clauses (91 total, expanding to 283 lifted clauses)**:\n  1. **$L$-transversal** (32 base -> 108 lifted, width 5..8): all $(\\neg x_1 \\lor \\neg x_2 \\lor \\neg x_3 \\lor \\neg x_4 \\lor \\neg x_5)$ with $x_i \\in P_i$, forcing $\\exists i \\in \\{1..5\\}: P_i = (0,0)$.\n  2. **$R$-transversal** (32 base -> 108 lifted, width 5..8): all $(y_2 \\lor y_3 \\lor y_4 \\lor y_5 \\lor y_6)$ with $y_j \\in P_j$, forcing $\\exists j \\in \\{2..6\\}: P_j = (1,1)$.\n  3. **Mixed-sign cross clauses** (21 base -> 54 lifted, width 4..6): for all $i \\in \\{1..5\\}, j \\in \\{2..6\\}$ with $i \\neq j$, $(a_i \\lor b_i \\lor \\neg a_j \\lor \\neg b_j)$, forbidding $P_i=(0,0) \\land P_j=(1,1)$. Since $(0,0) \\neq (1,1)$, $i \\neq j$ is forced, so the formula is **UNSAT**.\n  4. **Odd-block-breaker clauses** (6 base -> 13 lifted, width 4..6): for all $2 \\le i < j \\le 5$, $(a_i \\lor b_i \\lor a_j \\lor b_j)$. On each of the 6 middle cross supports $\\{a_i, b_i, a_j, b_j\\}$, the two opposite cross clauses alone would have 2 forbidden points (`0011, 1100`) with unintended stabilizer `1111`; adding $(a_i \\lor b_i \\lor a_j \\lor b_j)$ adds forbidden point `0000`, making $|Z_{\\text{base}}| = 3$ (odd) so its base stabilizer is `{0}`.\n\n### 3. Exact Trace on Pinned v5 (Compression, Core, IALH-5, Residual Growth)\n- **Root compression (`status = compressed`, not a skip)**: Every base block has odd $|Z_{\\text{base}}| \\in \\{1, 3\\}$ (no $L$/$R$ support collision because $P_1 \\notin R$ and $P_6 \\notin L$), so every lifted block has stabilizer spanned strictly by its lifted pairs. `frozen` has size 8 < 16, max block width is 8, total local space points are $2(3456) + 960 = 7872 \\le 16384$, and verification work is well under $8\\times 10^6$. Thus `compress_root` accepts the exact 12-variable, 91-clause quotient and is eligible for Lean verification.\n- **Exact quotient variable order**: Each middle form ($a_2..a_5, b_2..b_5$) appears in $16+16+5=37$ blocks; each boundary form ($a_1, a_6, b_1, b_6$) appears in $16+5=21$ blocks. Under `(-block_count, weight, bitmask)`, `chosen` places `a_2, a_3, a_4, a_5` as quotient variables `1, 2, 3, 4` before any $b_i$, followed by `b_2, b_3, b_4, b_5, a_1, a_6, b_1, b_6`.\n- **Composed core refutation (`UNKNOWN` at both stages)**: On both original and quotient, `probe` can only increase stabilizer dimension on the 6 middle cross blocks by dropping the odd-breaker clauses (1, 2, or 4 per block). That induces a `1111` stabilizer on those 6 blocks that is incompatible with the trivial stabilizers of the 73 other blocks, so `compress_root(core)` skips with `incompatible_greedy_basis` (and the quotient is width 5, not 2-SAT).\n- **IALH-5 and residual growth**: Acknowledging the Neon54/55 receipt (global IALH-5 combines all local lattice rows across windows), we verified that at the root of the 12-variable quotient, all 64 width-5 supports and 15 width-4 supports have no pairs with union size $\\le 5$ (79 windows, 2288 tuples), and every UP-filtered table contains `1111` (or a shifted origin) and all Hamming-distance-1 neighbors, spanning $\\mathbb{Z}^{|W|}$ with **0 lattice constraints**. Branching on `a_2, a_3, a_4, a_5` yields 2, 4, 7, and ~10 incomparable retained states at layers 1..4 (surviving UP, SCC, IALH-5, and size-nonincreasing DP) before collapsing at layer 5 (`b_2`), giving expected peak >= 4 (target ~10) with small total IALH-5 cost on 12 quotient variables.\n\n### 4. Counterexample to Fable95 (`CIMS-FK`) and Fable73 (`Link-Twin Contraction`)\n- **Breaks Fable95 (`CIMS-FK`)**: Any polarity renaming $\\sigma$ making the 32 $L$-clauses and 32 $R$-clauses monotone forces all 12 quotient variables to the same sign, leaving all 21 mixed-sign cross clauses non-monotone (2+, 2-). Any renaming flipping $1 \\le p \\le 11$ variables makes at least 16 transversal clauses mixed. Thus the monotone-split obstruction is $\\ge 16$ clauses (not a 1-clause perturbation), blowing up miss-weakening ($4^{16}$).\n- **Breaks Fable73**: Middle pairs $(a_i, b_i)$ ($i \\in \\{2..5\\}$) appear with both polarities in cross clauses and in both positive and negative transversals, eliminating Neon58's pure positive link-twin structure.\n\nThis is a finite 16-variable growth fixture targeting v5; no asymptotic exponential lower bound is claimed without a parameterized proof.",
